# The Bot's Core Conversation Flow

I would make this the actual backbone of the AI, rather than allowing it to randomly answer FAQs.

### INQUIRY

Client:
“Scientific logo design kya hota hai?”

Bot:
Explain Mantra → Tantra → Yantra → Business Yantra briefly.

Then immediately:

> “Aap apna naam aur business category share karenge? Saath mein current logo bhi bhej dijiye. Usse hum aapke case ko better understand kar paayenge.”

---

### LOGO RECEIVED

Bot:

> “Thank you Sir. Aapka logo mil gaya. Aapke business mein currently sabse bada challenge kya hai—payment, sales, deals, staff ya overall growth?”

This is a high-value qualification question.

---

### CLIENT GIVES PAIN

For example:

> “Payment stuck hai.”

Bot:

> “Understood Sir. Payment-related issue ko logo ke perspective se bhi analyse kiya ja sakta hai. Existing identity mein kuch visual/energetic factors business ke desired payment flow ko support kar rahe hain ya nahi, yeh dekhna relevant rahega.”

Then:

> “Maulik personally 15-minute Zoom mein aapka logo analyse karke observations explain kar sakte hain. Kya aap Zoom ke liye convenient rahenge?”

---

### CLIENT DOESN'T WANT ZOOM

Don't push.

Say:

> “No problem Sir. Aap mujhe analysis ke liye kal tak ka time dijiye. Main relevant observations check karke aapse reconnect karunga. Uske baad aap khud decide kijiye ki observations aapke business se relate karte hain ya nahi.”

This creates curiosity + trust + permission, rather than pressure.

---

### CLIENT ASKS PRICE TOO EARLY

Don't hide the price, but don't make price the centre of the conversation:

> “Scientific Logo Design ki fee ₹50,004 hai. Lekin usse pehle hum recommend karenge ki aapka existing logo aur business challenge samajh liya jaye, kyunki yeh normal logo designing project nahi hai. Agar aap apna logo aur business category share kar dein, toh next step personally Maulik ke saath 15-minute analysis rakh sakte hain.”

---

## One important positioning principle

The bot should never say:

> “Aapka payment logo ki wajah se stuck hai.”

Instead:

> “Payment issue ko logo ke perspective se bhi analyse karna relevant ho sakta hai.”

And never:

> “Logo change karoge toh sales badh jayegi.”

Instead:

> “Scientific Logo Design ka objective business ki visual identity ko desired growth direction ke saath align karna hai.”

This keeps the communication strong, credible and consultative, while still creating the curiosity needed to get the prospect into the Zoom meeting.

Most importantly, the bot should not give the complete diagnosis on WhatsApp. The valuable moment is when the prospect sits with Maulik for 15 minutes and hears, personally, what is happening in their existing logo. That is where the trust, authority and conversion opportunity should peak.